data.content:
Here's the solution using two files:

**How it works:**

1. **`GlobalExceptionHandler.cs`** — Implements `IExceptionHandler` (built-in since .NET 8). It pattern-matches exception types to status codes and writes a `ProblemDetails` JSON response. No sensitive details leak on 500s.

2. **`ProgramSetup.cs`** — Shows the two lines to add to your `Program.cs`:
   ```csharp
   builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();
   builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<GlobalExceptionHandler>();
   // then in the pipeline:
   app.UseExceptionHandler();
   app.UseStatusCodePages();
   ```

**Example 404 response:**
```json
{
  "type": "https://httpstatuses.com/404",
  "title": "Resource Not Found",
  "status": 404,
  "detail": "Item not found."
}
```

No try-catch in endpoints — the middleware catches everything globally. If you're on .NET 6/7 instead of 8+, you'd use `app.UseExceptionHandler(...)` with a lambda and `IExceptionHandlerFeature`, but `IExceptionHandler` is the cleaner modern approach.
